caption: Eldritch Modifier
domain-rule: eldritch-modifier

Eldritch, -5%, is the mature source modifier for powers whose Psi and Super components have fully fused. It is not available merely for entering the Domain or reaching a particular Eldritch Rating. Mastery grants access to Eldritch under the General Origin Rules: traits purchased through a mastered Eldritch Gifts Tradition may replace Psionic, -10%, plus Super, -10%, with Eldritch, -5%, and later purchases through that mastered Tradition may use Eldritch from the time of purchase. The character pays the normal character-point difference when converting an existing trait.

An Eldritch ability is simultaneously Psi and Super for countermeasure purposes, but cannot be shut down by only one side. Neutralize, Static, anti-power abilities, wards, suppressive technology, or similar countermeasures must be effective against both Psi and Super to affect a trait with Eldritch. Two separate countermeasures may satisfy this requirement if both are actually affecting the ability at the same time. A countermeasure explicitly defined as affecting Eldritch counts as satisfying both requirements.

Eldritch replaces Psionic and Super rather than stacking with either of them. A trait with Eldritch is no longer separately Psionic or Super for source-modifier pricing, although it still counts as both where Domain or Tradition rules classify its nature.
